IMPORT prelude

-- Property Tax Act 1960 (Singapore) -- the charge and its exemptions (s 6), the statutory rate (s 9), owners' notices
-- (s 19), objections and appeals (ss 20A, 29), paying despite an objection (s 35A), the late-payment penalty (s 36), the
-- seller who gives no notice (s 47), and the owner's deduction from rent (s 6(10), (11)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments to
-- Act 33 of 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 36 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, 24 of them for s 10 (the Valuation
-- List): other Acts measure their own charges by annual value. SCOPED to the owner's obligations and remedies. Not
-- encoded: administration, valuation by gross receipts, the Valuation Review Board's constitution and procedure, recovery
-- by attachment and sale, street and building names (Part 6), offences, and the rate orders under s 9(2), which set the
-- rates actually paid by most owners and were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Property Tax Act 1960 -- the owner`

§§ `6, 9 -- the charge`

-- s 2: "annual value" of a building or land is "the gross amount at which the same can reasonably be expected to be let
-- from year to year, the landlord paying the expenses of repair, insurance, maintenance or upkeep and all taxes (other
-- than goods and services tax)".
-- s 6(1), (2): tax on the annual value of everything in the Valuation List, payable by the OWNER "yearly in advance
-- without demand, in the month of January". (4): "a first charge on the property". (5): "No tax is payable on any [property]
-- the annual value of which is $18 or less."
-- s 9(1): "at the rate of 36% upon the annual value". (2): the Minister may set lower rates by order for prescribed
-- properties. (The owner-occupier and other progressive rates are in such orders; none was retrieved, so the rate is a
-- parameter, defaulting to the statutory 36%.)
-- s 6(6): a building or part "used EXCLUSIVELY" (a) for public religious worship, (b) for a grant-aided public school,
-- (c) for charitable purposes, or (d) for purposes conducive to social development, is exempt.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory rate` MEANS 0.36

GIVEN `annual value` IS A NUMBER, `rate` IS A NUMBER, `exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax for the year` MEANS
    IF `exempt` OR `annual value` AT MOST 18
    THEN 0
    ELSE `annual value` TIMES `rate`

DECLARE Use HAS
    `used exclusively for worship, a grant-aided school, charity or social development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `also used partly for commercial letting` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building or part is exempt under section 6(6)` IF
        `the use`'s `used exclusively for worship, a grant-aided school, charity or social development`
    AND NOT `the use`'s `also used partly for commercial letting`

§§ `6(10), (11) -- deducting the tax from rent the owner pays`

-- s 6(10): where premises are held subject to the owner's payment of "any rent, rentcharge, annuity or other like
-- payment", the owner who has paid the tax may, "DESPITE ANY STIPULATION TO THE CONTRARY", deduct from that payment a sum
-- bearing "the same proportion to the tax so paid ... as the amount of that rent ... bears to the annual value". (11):
-- not from rent payable to the Government or a public authority.
--
-- An owner holding under a private ground lease passes part of the property tax up to the ground landlord, and no clause
-- in the lease can stop it.
GIVEN `tax paid` IS A NUMBER, `rent paid by the owner` IS A NUMBER, `annual value` IS A NUMBER, `rent is to the Government or a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction the owner may make` MEANS
    IF `rent is to the Government or a public authority` OR `annual value` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `tax paid` TIMES `rent paid by the owner` DIVIDED BY `annual value`

§§ `19, 47 -- the seller's notice`

-- s 19(1): on a sale or transfer the vendor "must, within ONE MONTH after the sale or transfer ... give notice thereof to
-- the Chief Assessor". s 47(1): every seller "continues to be liable for the payment of all taxes payable in respect of
-- the property ... which become payable ... at any time before the notice of transfer ... has been given". (2): the buyer's
-- liability is unaffected. And s 6(4): the tax is a first charge on the property.
--
-- A seller who never gives notice remains liable for tax falling due after completion -- next January's tax included --
-- jointly with the buyer, whose property carries the charge.
GIVEN `tax fell due before the seller's notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller remains liable for the tax` IF
    `tax fell due before the seller's notice`

GIVEN `days since completion` IS A NUMBER, `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller is late with the notice` IF
    `days since completion` GREATER THAN 30 AND NOT `notice given`

-- s 19(3): notice of demolition within 15 days. (4): where a building is demolished "and no action has been taken to
-- amend the Valuation List in respect thereof FOR ANY REASON", the owner must, "at the option of the Comptroller", either
-- (a) continue to pay "as if the building had not been demolished", or (b) pay from the demolition date on any revised
-- annual value later ascribed.
--
-- "For any reason" includes the Chief Assessor's own inaction after a timely notice. Limb (a) is at the Comptroller's
-- option, not the owner's.
GIVEN `the building was demolished` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Valuation List was amended` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner gave timely notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Comptroller may tax the demolished building as standing` IF
    `the building was demolished` AND NOT `the Valuation List was amended`

§§ `20A, 29 -- objections and appeals`

-- s 20A(1): an owner may object to the inclusion of a property or its annual value "at any time in that year". (2): an
-- objection to an AMENDMENT made under s 20 must be within 30 days of the notice. (5): if allowed, the Chief Assessor may
-- specify "any date in the year in which the objection is made" from which it takes effect. (7): appeal to the Valuation
-- Review Board within 30 days, but only against a decision that DISALLOWED the objection or allowed it IN PART.
-- s 29(4): a late appeal may be allowed for absence from Singapore, sickness or other reasonable cause, without
-- unreasonable delay.
DECLARE Objection HAS
    `against an amendment under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since the amendment notice` IS A NUMBER
    `made in the year the value applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the objection` IS AN Objection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is in time` IF
    IF `the objection`'s `against an amendment under section 20`
    THEN `the objection`'s `days since the amendment notice` AT MOST 30
    ELSE `the objection`'s `made in the year the value applies`

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `disallowed`
    `allowed in whole`
    `allowed in part`
    `allowed as agreed`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN Outcome, `days since the decision notice` IS A NUMBER, `late for reasonable cause without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Valuation Review Board lies` IF
        (CONSIDER `the outcome`
            WHEN `disallowed` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `allowed in part` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (`days since the decision notice` AT MOST 30 OR `late for reasonable cause without unreasonable delay`)

§§ `35A, 36 -- pay first, and the penalty`

-- s 35A(1): tax on the annual value in the List is payable "even if" a remission application, a claim, or "an objection
-- or appeal" is pending.
-- s 36(1): unpaid at the prescribed time, "a sum not exceeding 5% of the amount of outstanding tax is to be added". (2):
-- remissible for good cause.
GIVEN `an objection or appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tax must still be paid on time` IF
    TRUE

GIVEN `outstanding tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum late-payment penalty` MEANS
    `outstanding tax` TIMES 0.05

-- s 6(14), (15): a refund of tax overpaid must be claimed "within 5 years of such excess payment".
GIVEN `years since the excess payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refund claim is in time` IF
    `years since the excess payment` AT MOST 5
